  message: "DONE BY WI-jojaf (PR #794, INV-nular F7), 2026-09-06. Owner authorised the\nfold in the owner-decision walk-through on condition that the assumptions\nwere checked first; checked against the tip and the WI-nolut instrument\n(~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jsleg_completeness_09062026/), not recalled.\nThis item's three asks, each against evidence:\n  1. fs reads rowed AND reachable in idiom: compare.out shows NO-FSREAD\n     `violated` in BOTH arms for all 11 javascript cohort repos\n     (automerge-repo, express, ioredis, knex, mastodon,\n     openzeppelin-contracts, pm2, polis, rollup, winston, y-sweet), so an\n     fs_read crossing stayed represented in every repo after the seven\n     path rows were deleted. INV-misup (the javascript dead-row cause this\n     item named) is satisfied.\n  2. finding-level A/B on real node repos, both arms cold: arm.sh creates a\n     FRESH XDG_CACHE_HOME per repo per arm (a new directory, cold by\n     construction), old arm on the javascript.yaml.old snapshot; 0 of 44\n     verdict categories moved; the deletion removed no fs_read verdict\n     anywhere, which is exactly the relocate-not-delete question this item\n     said the erlang analogue did not settle for javascript. Mechanical\n     confirmation before deletion: probe.js read NO I/O signal on join,\n     dirname, basename, extname, relative, normalize; resolve flagged only\n     on process.cwd(), which is rowed on process.\n  3. ADJACENCY_KNOWN_UNFIXED updated: the set is EMPTY at tip with the dated\n     comment naming this deletion, and\n     test_the_known_unfixed_entry_still_describes_a_live_row guards it.\n     Pinned: TestF7PurePathArithmeticIsNoLongerARead (classify_call None for\n     each; realpath control still fs_read); `path` is a completeness grant\n     dated 2026-09-06.\nNot a proxy closure: the verdict table and the probe output are the\nbehavioural evidence; the exemption set is the bookkeeping."  # 372b
